last_played": 1768749807, "avatar": "59d1f01ac26f82407ade6fe9ce396e5d5677181a"}, "language": "english", "review": "I had an unbelievable amount of time spent in 2. It took me a while, but I eventually made the jump over to 3. Comparing the two is incredibly difficult. At the end of the day, you can't go wrong with either. The sheer volume of content in 2 is something that cannot be topped, but there is something that just feels better when you're playing 3. Just that little bit of modernity goes a long way. I also feel that the editor is much quicker and easier to use as well. Jumping into these titles without prior knowledge would be an absolute culture shock and nightmare lol. It's clunky, janky, and riddled with bugs and issues. But my god once you get a grip on it, once it starts to click and you begin to form some modicum of control, it's an experience like no other. You can truly lose yourself here. I'm an immersion based rpg player at heart and these games completely scratch that itch. There's really no sense in attempting to go into details like an actual thoughtful review because this is something that you just have to play, you just have to engross yourself in it and at the end of that path lies one of my top favorite games of all time- a game like no other. 2 or 3, it doesn't matter, get whichever is cheaper.", "timestamp_created": 1762528911, "timestamp_updated": 1762528911, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.54624021053314209", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 22, "count": 1}]}]}